# Dev Loops

Keep the inner loop fast so agents iterate on real behavior instead of waiting on Docker or full builds. Each tier has an explicit time budget and script.

| Tier | Budget | Purpose | WSL script | Windows launcher |
|------|--------|---------|------------|------------------|
| **Fast** | **< 15s** | Unit + shared widget sanity while editing | `flutter test test/data test/shared` | (run from WSL) |
| **Feature** | **< 90s** cold, **< 15s** warm | Full analyze + test + dev server on :3000 | `bash scripts/wsl_dev.sh` | `dev-local.cmd` / `dev-local.ps1` |
| **Pre-push** | **< 15m** | Tier 1 + `flutter build web` + docker/nginx :8080 + deep-link smoke + coverage gate | `bash scripts/wsl_deploy.sh` | `deploy-local.cmd` / `deploy-local.ps1` |
| **Ship** | **< 15m** | Tier 1 + Tier 2 smoke (teardown) + push + GitHub PR to `main` | `bash scripts/wsl_ship_branch.sh` | `ship-branch.cmd` / `ship-branch.ps1` |
| **CI** | ≤ pipeline SLA | GitHub Actions → GitHub Pages (static) | (not local) | (default-branch push) |

## Rules

- **Docker is forbidden in the Fast and Feature tiers.** Use the Flutter dev server on :3000 for UI iteration.
- **Coverage gate lives in the Pre-push tier** — `scripts/wsl_coverage.sh` runs `flutter test --coverage` and enforces (calibrated to 2026-07-10 baseline, aspirational targets in parens):
  - `lib/data/services/**` line coverage `>= 60%` (aspirational 70%)
  - `lib/shared/utils/**`  line coverage `>= 60%` (already at ~74%)
  - `lib/**` (overall)     line coverage `>= 45%` (aspirational 50%)
  - Override via env vars (`SERVICES_THRESHOLD=70 ...`) or edit the script when tests catch up.
  - Optionally wire the same script into CI later; local pre-push remains the gate.
- Prefer `dev-local.cmd` when only iterating; run `deploy-local.cmd` only before commit / push or after routing/deploy changes.
- Run `ship-branch.cmd` when commits are ready for review (Tier 1 + Tier 2 + push + PR); it tears down Docker unlike `deploy-local`.
- If the Fast tier exceeds 15s, narrow the test scope; do not silently move to the Feature tier.
- If the Pre-push tier exceeds 15m, split the change or defer non-essential work to the next branch.

## Time budgets are a signal

- **Fast tier > 15s** → excessive service-test setup or async wait; extract test doubles.
- **Feature tier > 90s cold** → oversized `flutter pub get` or asset regen; check for stale caches or wide `pub upgrade`.
- **Pre-push tier > 15m** → Docker cache miss or missing `docker pull` warmup; check `scripts/wsl_deploy.sh` prewarm.

## Cross-reference

- `dev-local.cmd` → `scripts/wsl_dev.sh` (Tier 1 + Flutter dev server)
- `deploy-local.cmd` → `scripts/wsl_deploy.sh` (Tier 2 + coverage gate; leaves Docker running)
- `ship-branch.cmd` → `scripts/wsl_ship_branch.sh` (Tier 1 + Tier 2 smoke + push + PR; tears down Docker)
- Shared helpers live in `scripts/wsl_common.sh`
